How apps/admin finds your SonarCloud token. sonar-local.sh and
fetch-sonar-issues.command both resolve it through sonar-token.sh, in this order:

  1. the SONAR_TOKEN environment variable
  2. the login Keychain, service name "sonar-token-superadmin"
  3. a gitignored ".sonar-token" file in this folder (legacy)

Generate a token at: https://sonarcloud.io/account/security

Prefer the Keychain. It keeps the token off disk in plaintext and every checkout
on the machine picks it up, so there is nothing to copy into a new worktree:

  security add-generic-password -a "$USER" -s sonar-token-superadmin -w <your-token> -U

For a single shell, or for anything driven over ssh — where the login keychain is
locked and the Keychain read returns nothing — export it instead:

  export SONAR_TOKEN=<your-token>

Option 3 still works so an unmigrated checkout keeps running, but it writes your
token to disk in plaintext. If you already have a .sonar-token file, move it into
the Keychain with the command above and then delete the file.
